                <pb facs="0716" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2976: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shaw</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-01T17:00:00+00:00">December 1, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 1—1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>825. From Ambassador Dawes: Referring to Department’s No. 609 of November
                        30.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d564-f1"/> The Italian representative called upon
                    me this noon in regard to a delegate of his country joining the commission, and
                    I informed Scialoja in the Under Secretary’s words that my Government would
                    naturally not object to an Italian member on the commission, since its
                    appointment is entirely a League of Nations matter. [Dawes.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shaw</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
